What's the matter with you?

975
01:16:23.087 --> 01:16:24.672
Why do you like me, Charlotte?

976
01:16:29.594 --> 01:16:30.595
What do you mean?

977
01:16:33.180 --> 01:16:36.058
-I like you 'cause I like you.
-No. Really.

978
01:16:37.059 --> 01:16:38.227
Why do you like me?

979
01:16:40.229 --> 01:16:41.898
Who wouldn't like that guy?

980
01:16:44.609 --> 01:16:46.194
That's not me, Charlotte.

981
01:16:47.612 --> 01:16:48.863
It was a joke.

982
01:16:54.160 --> 01:16:57.079
Just because you went to Kenya
for five days,

983
01:16:57.955 --> 01:17:00.917
doesn't mean you understand who I am.

984
01:17:12.345 --> 01:17:14.096
You know what your problem is, Barry?

985
01:17:14.513 --> 01:17:17.600
You think that this... is all about you.

986
01:17:21.896 --> 01:17:22.981
Good night.

987
01:17:51.343 --> 01:17:54.595
- What happened to your face?
-I don't wanna talk about it.

988
01:18:01.979 --> 01:18:04.272
Man, listen, um...

989
01:18:04.356 --> 01:18:08.818
one of the guys at Robbie's suite
just moved out, so...

990
01:18:08.901 --> 01:18:10.362
there's a room open.

991
01:18:13.698 --> 01:18:16.450
-You should take it.
-Are you sure? I...

992
01:18:16.784 --> 01:18:18.661
I know you can afford the rent
by yourself.

993
01:18:18.744 --> 01:18:21.081
-I just thought--
-I'm ready for a change anyway.

994
01:18:21.164 --> 01:18:22.374
Yeah.

995
01:18:23.290 --> 01:18:24.458
No, I...

996
01:18:25.085 --> 01:18:26.461
I can move in with Saleem.

997
01:18:29.755 --> 01:18:32.717
I just feel isolated from campus,
you know?

998
01:18:32.800 --> 01:18:35.303
It's cool, Will. I get it.

999
01:18:42.560 --> 01:18:44.812
-We'll still hang out, right?
-Yeah. Of course.

1000
01:21:40.905 --> 01:21:42.698
Barry, my brother.

1001
01:21:43.782 --> 01:21:45.743
We live in a shithole, you know that?

1002
01:21:46.785 --> 01:21:49.456
I mean, an actual place for shitting.

1003
01:21:50.498 --> 01:21:52.500
All afternoon, I am watching

1004
01:21:52.583 --> 01:21:55.211
white people bring their dogs here
to shit.

1005
01:21:56.213 --> 01:21:59.924
And they just walk away.
They just leave the shit.

1006
01:22:02.092 --> 01:22:04.596
Look, look, here comes another one now.

1007
01:22:04.679 --> 01:22:08.974
Hey! Clean up after your filthy animal,
you filthy animal!

1008
01:22:10.017 --> 01:22:12.687
Bedtime for Saleem. Come on. Come on.

1009
01:22:12.770 --> 01:22:14.104
Come on.

1010
01:22:17.317 --> 01:22:19.151
I like that girl Charlotte, Barry.

1011
01:22:20.736 --> 01:22:23.072
She called a bit earlier.

1012
01:22:24.949 --> 01:22:27.743
She said she was gonna pick you up
at noon for the wedding.

1013
01:22:31.747 --> 01:22:33.165
-Hey, Barry?
-Yeah?

1014
01:22:34.833 --> 01:22:36.877
You're becoming a real bore.

1015
01:23:12.289 --> 01:23:15.625
-Hello?
- Barry? Is that you?

1016
01:23:15.709 --> 01:23:17.585
Yes. Who's this?

1017
01:23:17.669 --> 01:23:21.213
Yes, Barry, this is your Aunt Jane,
in Nairobi.

1018
01:23:21.297 --> 01:23:22.464
Can you hear me?

1019
01:23:22.548 --> 01:23:25.718
Uh, barely. I'm sorry, my aunt who?

1020
01:23:25.801 --> 01:23:27.761
Aunt Jane.

1021
01:23:28.471 --> 01:23:33.435
Listen, Barry, your father is dead.
He is killed in a car accident.

1022
01:23:35.185 --> 01:23:39.399
Hello? Can you hear me?
I said your father is dead.

1023
01:23:39.482 --> 01:23:42.276
Please call your uncle in Boston
and tell him.

1024
01:23:42.360 --> 01:23:46.740
I cannot talk now, okay, Barry?
I will try to call you again.

1025
01:24:16.101 --> 01:24:21.358
Okay, so, don't laugh, but I'm thinking
of taking a job on Wall Street.

1026
01:24:23.859 --> 01:24:28.405
Daddy's got some friends.
I'm just sick of being broke, man.

1027
01:24:28.740 --> 01:24:31.451
It's getting lame. What do you think?

1028
01:24:37.289 --> 01:24:38.415
Oh, that's it?

1029
01:24:38.832 --> 01:24:43.003
No "you'll fit in great with the rest
of those cokehead assholes"?

1030
01:24:43.253 --> 01:24:47.509
No "if you actually stood for anything,
I'd call you a sellout"?

1031
01:24:51.053 --> 01:24:54.264
Ah, you're becoming a real bore,
have I mentioned that?

1032
01:25:07.236 --> 01:25:08.987
It's like musical chairs or--

1033
01:25:09.071 --> 01:25:14.828
I mean, you turn 25, the music stops,
and whoever you're dating, you marry?

1034
01:25:16.245 --> 01:25:19.373
It's not just my sister, either.
It's all of her friends--

1035
01:25:19.457 --> 01:25:21.835
I don't see them for a few months,
and then, bam,

1036
01:25:21.917 --> 01:25:25.337
they show up with rocks on their fingers
and some random guy in tow.

1037
01:25:25.422 --> 01:25:28.675
And it's like, "Wow, what a coincidence."

1038
01:25:28.758 --> 01:25:30.342
You all just happened
to meet your soulmates

1039
01:25:30.426 --> 01:25:32.219
within six months of each other?

1040
01:25:33.471 --> 01:25:34.681
What are the odds?"

1041
01:25:41.145 --> 01:25:41.937
Hey.

1042
01:25:45.775 --> 01:25:47.234
You feel really far away.

1043
01:25:48.610 --> 01:25:49.111
Sorry.

1044
01:25:56.326 --> 01:25:57.662
Not what I meant.

1045
01:26:04.168 --> 01:26:06.086
Do you hate weddings or something?

1046
01:26:07.755 --> 01:26:09.256
No, I've never even been to a wedding,

1047
01:26:11.383 --> 01:26:12.719
except for my mother's.

1048
01:26:14.970 --> 01:26:16.681
Well, would you ever want to get married?

1049
01:26:20.142 --> 01:26:23.437
I don't mean now.
I don't even mean to me.

1050
01:26:23.521 --> 01:26:27.942
I just mean... is it something
you could see yourself doing someday?

1051
01:26:29.359 --> 01:26:33.030
No, it's, uh, not an institution
I put much faith in.

1052
01:26:34.699 --> 01:26:38.327
I mean, my parents were married five times
between them. Or six.

1053
01:26:38.410 --> 01:26:40.162
And I'm not even sure about my father.

1054
01:26:46.460 --> 01:26:49.963
Well... are you nervous
about meeting my family?

1055
01:26:55.385 --> 01:26:57.262
-Why? Do I look nervous to you?
-No.

1056
01:27:02.810 --> 01:27:04.311
You look like you're going into battle.

1057
01:27:25.415 --> 01:27:26.918
All right, big smiles!

1058
01:27:28.669 --> 01:27:31.088
Now, hold it! Hold it!
One more. Just one more.

1059
01:27:32.548 --> 01:27:33.340
Come on.

1060
01:27:35.593 --> 01:27:37.679
Great. All right, all the fellas.

1061
01:27:38.387 --> 01:27:41.056
Yeah, Barry, come. Come join us.

1062
01:27:41.558 --> 01:27:44.894
-You stand with Martin, here.
- Hello.

1063
01:27:44.978 --> 01:27:46.270
Hey, George.

1064
01:27:47.437 --> 01:27:49.439
There's the man.

1065
01:27:49.523 --> 01:27:53.110
-Yep, okay.
-It's kind of an uptight crowd, huh?

1066
01:27:53.694 --> 01:27:54.987
I'm kind of an uptight guy.

1067
01:27:59.324 --> 01:28:01.743
Great! Now all the ladies.

1068
01:28:18.720 --> 01:28:19.929
Ready?

1069
01:28:22.723 --> 01:28:26.143
It's the second time this week.
The second.

1070
01:28:26.644 --> 01:28:30.272
Listen, you have to take it easy.
You know they're not like back home.

1071
01:28:33.025 --> 01:28:33.817
Hello, sir.

1072
01:28:35.193 --> 01:28:39.949
-Can I get you something?
-No, no. I'm just, um, I'm killing time.

1073
01:28:55.006 --> 01:28:56.214
How you guys doing today?

1074
01:28:57.549 --> 01:28:58.508
Fine, sir.

1075
01:29:01.804 --> 01:29:04.057
-My name's Barry.
-Fred.

1076
01:29:05.099 --> 01:29:06.266
Ephraim.

1077
01:29:13.440 --> 01:29:16.276
-Where you guys from?
-We are Ugandan.

1078
01:29:17.444 --> 01:29:18.904
I thought so.

1079
01:29:20.155 --> 01:29:22.532
My, uh... father is from Kenya.

1080
01:29:22.616 --> 01:29:24.326
Ah!

1081
01:29:25.619 --> 01:29:26.871
Here you go.

1082
01:29:26.953 --> 01:29:28.080
Yeah. He...

1083
01:29:29.331 --> 01:29:30.624
He died recently.

1084
01:29:31.793 --> 01:29:34.461
My condolences to you and to your family.

1085
01:29:34.544 --> 01:29:35.672
Mine as well.

1086
01:29:37.297 --> 01:29:38.507
Yeah, thanks.

1087
01:29:40.802 --> 01:29:42.260
Yeah. It was today, actually.

1088
01:29:43.887 --> 01:29:44.513
I, uh...

1089
01:29:46.015 --> 01:29:50.310
I got a phone call this morning
from, uh, from an aunt I never met.

1090
01:29:59.861 --> 01:30:04.032
Actually, you know what?
I will have a drink.

1091
01:30:07.161 --> 01:30:10.873
-What do you got back there?
-It's a full bar, sir.

1092
01:30:13.041 --> 01:30:13.917
I'll have a...

1093
01:30:15.044 --> 01:30:16.378
I'll have a vodka.

1094
01:30:40.986 --> 01:30:41.570
Cheers.

1095
01:30:52.539 --> 01:30:54.876
-How you doing?

1096
01:31:04.634 --> 01:31:07.096
-Yeah, this is my boyfriend, Barry.
- Oh, hi.

1097
01:31:07.180 --> 01:31:08.806
-Barry.
-Good to meet you.

1098
01:31:08.890 --> 01:31:11.600
-Barry, this is Donna.
-Barry.

1099
01:31:11.683 --> 01:31:13.602
-Ted.
-Barry.

1100
01:31:13.685 --> 01:31:15.270
-And Emily.
-Pleasure.

1101
01:31:16.022 --> 01:31:19.483
-Oh, and this is my cousin, Melissa.
-Barry.

1102
01:31:20.442 --> 01:31:21.610
Hey.

1103
01:31:22.527 --> 01:31:25.739
Barry, there's someone
I'm dying to introduce you to.

1104
01:31:25.823 --> 01:31:27.574
-Just when I thought I'd met everyone.
-Hmm.

1105
01:31:42.672 --> 01:31:46.010
Barry, meet James and Grace Lee.

1106
01:31:46.093 --> 01:31:49.596
Two of the most brilliant,
committed writers and activists

1107
01:31:49.679 --> 01:31:52.183
-I have ever had the pleasure to know.
-Well, I'm honored to meet you.

1108
01:31:52.975 --> 01:31:56.979
Grace Lee tried to convince Malcolm X
to run for Senate in '64.

1109
01:31:57.063 --> 01:31:59.439
-It almost worked, too.
- Wow.

1110
01:32:00.107 --> 01:32:03.027
I thought you might want to meet them.
Especially because of your parents.

1111
01:32:07.824 --> 01:32:08.950
Have a seat, Barry.

1112
01:32:12.245 --> 01:32:13.453
Are your parents in the movement?

1113
01:32:13.537 --> 01:32:15.539
Uh, no. Not really.

1114
01:32:16.081 --> 01:32:19.709
They're, uh, different races.
I'm guessing that's what Kathy meant.

1115
01:32:20.710 --> 01:32:22.712
Ah, I see.

1116
01:32:23.755 --> 01:32:28.802
My mom's from Kansas,
and my dad's from Kenya.

1117
01:32:31.055 --> 01:32:32.849
I've only met him once, though.

1118
01:32:34.058 --> 01:32:36.476
I grew up in Jakarta and Honolulu,

1119
01:32:36.560 --> 01:32:41.065
and spent a little time in California,
then, well, I ended up here.

1120
01:32:42.357 --> 01:32:43.608
That's some kinda gumbo.

1121
01:32:47.071 --> 01:32:48.488
You know what that makes you,
young brother?

1122
01:32:49.531 --> 01:32:52.034
No, sir.  I don't.

1123
01:32:52.117 --> 01:32:54.244
I really, really don't.

1124
01:32:55.579 --> 01:32:59.416
It makes you American.
And you don't ever have to choose.

1125
01:33:05.505 --> 01:33:10.385
You know, I see you both
sitting here together, in love.

1126
01:33:11.469 --> 01:33:13.471
-Yes, sir.
-And full of wisdom.

1127
01:33:13.972 --> 01:33:15.849
And I can't help but think that...

1128
01:33:16.558 --> 01:33:18.602
the two of you must have been
through all kinds of hell together.

1129
01:33:18.685 --> 01:33:22.856
Doing what you've done.
And looking how you look.

1130
01:33:22.940 --> 01:33:25.734
You take the baton
from the ones who've come before,

1131
01:33:25.817 --> 01:33:28.069
and you carry it as far as you can.

1132
01:33:28.528 --> 01:33:29.905
And then you hand it off.

1133
01:33:31.239 --> 01:33:33.742
That's life. A beautiful struggle.

1134
01:33:56.514 --> 01:33:57.557
Hey.

1135
01:34:00.394 --> 01:34:01.603
Dance with me.

1136
01:36:59.948 --> 01:37:01.032
"Dear Dad,

1137
01:37:02.368 --> 01:37:05.162
I am sorry it has taken me so long
to write you back.

1138
01:37:06.663 --> 01:37:09.250
I have thought of you
and your invitation to visit every day.

1139
01:37:10.209 --> 01:37:13.044
Sometimes I feel
that there's a part of me I do not know,

1140
01:37:14.963 --> 01:37:16.549
and when I am feeling optimistic,

1141
01:37:16.631 --> 01:37:19.218
I find myself believing that you hold
the answers I am looking for.

1142
01:37:21.386 --> 01:37:24.139
My journey so far has not been
as dramatic as yours,

1143
01:37:24.556 --> 01:37:27.809
but I'd like to think I can imagine
what you felt when you arrived in Hawaii.

1144
01:37:28.561 --> 01:37:30.937
Perhaps even what you felt
when you met Mom.

1145
01:37:32.856 --> 01:37:36.693
I suppose I have spent these last months
in New York trying to find my way.

1146
01:37:37.068 --> 01:37:39.070
Maybe that is all any of us do.

1147
01:37:40.738 --> 01:37:42.949
I look forward to discussing
these things with you, Dad.

1148
01:37:44.242 --> 01:37:46.286
It is high time we got to know each other.

1149
01:37:48.121 --> 01:37:50.915
Love, Barack."

1150
01:39:01.736 --> 01:39:02.612
Hey.

1151
01:39:04.656 --> 01:39:05.365
You wanna play Horse?

1152
01:39:05.865 --> 01:39:08.034
-Sure.
-You can shoot first.

1153
01:39:11.538 --> 01:39:12.997
Oh, okay.

1154
01:39:14.832 --> 01:39:16.584
Woo! Nice one.

1155
01:39:26.261 --> 01:39:27.011
I got an H.

1156
01:39:29.640 --> 01:39:31.725
-Right here.
-Okay.

1157
01:39:35.353 --> 01:39:38.606
Pretty good. Good. Guess I'm up.

1158
01:39:42.694 --> 01:39:43.736
Where you from?

1159
01:39:44.446 --> 01:39:49.158
-Riverside. How 'bout you?
-I'm from a lot of places.

1160
01:39:49.242 --> 01:39:51.786
But I... I live here now.
